                <pb facs="0061" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg55"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby, chargé, to
                        Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pelting</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-07"><hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 22.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I received
                    to-day a telegram from Consul Fowler, Ningpo, stating that the Taotai persists
                    in closing the port to all ships.</p>
                <p>As Japan, however, has given no pledge not to attack Ningpo, I have telegraphed
                    him in reply that this legation “can not object to China’s necessary defensive
                    measures.”</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. Denby</hi>, Jr.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
